fact because that retrieval went through WebFetch instead of retrieval_log.fetch, which is how a claim about a retrieval came to rest on nothing a later reader could check. Also: this row says seven routes; ten attempts were made and three were unpersisted. || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: RC1/RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26): result-payload link(s) derived from this search''s own query_text against the retrieval log, per section 2.1''s rule. (1 artefact(s)) || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: result artefact(s) added: retrieval-log/session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining/32ed63159c77e21e.html' WHERE "exec_id" = 72;
UPDATE "search_executions" SET "findings_note" = 'PREDICTION MET, AND THIS IS THE PREDICTOR FIRST PROSPECTIVE TEST RATHER THAN A THIRD RETROSPECTIVE OBSERVATION. Predicted >= 8 of the references would match; 19 OF 30 DO. The prediction was written into the deferral note in batch 16 and into this batch priors file, both committed before the pass ran, so it is a test and not a description. GAP-018 asked for three or four such passes before the predictor is treated as doctrine; this is one, and it should be counted as one rather than as confirmation. WHAT THE SEAM CONTAINS: the propulsion-on-slopes literature almost in full -- kinetic analysis on indoor and outdoor surfaces, uphill handrim biomechanics, load on the upper extremity, EMG during paraplegic propulsion, and TWO 1989 portable-ramp papers (10.1177/030802268905201209 and 10.3109/03790798909166390, the latter already staged as candidate 101 in batch 16, which is a cross-confirmation that the two anchors reference sets overlap where the predictor says they should). DEPTH-1: nothing discovered here is mined in this pass. || CORRECTED 2026-09-18: RETRACTED. This note opens PREDICTION MET, 19 OF 30. The 19 is a SCREEN ARTEFACT: the screen carried ''propuls'' and ''accessib'', so any wheelchair-propulsion paper matched regardless of slope, and REF-00979 IS a propulsion paper. Derive it rather than quoting either figure: python3 scripts/research/mining_screen.py --ref REF-00979 --compare. GAP-029 carries the retraction; GAP-018 and GAP-027 are superseded. The prediction was neither met nor missed -- it was scored on an instrument that could not measure it. || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26 5.2d): mined_ref_id derived -- this row''s own query_text names exactly one REF id that exists in evidence_sources. || RC1/RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26): result-payload link(s) derived from this search''s own query_text against the retrieval log, per section 2.1''s rule. (1 artefact(s)) || CORRECTED 2026-0