UPDATE "search_executions" SET "findings_note" = 'PRIOR SLIGHTLY LOW ON COUNT (5 of 25, predicted 0-2) AND EXACTLY RIGHT ON CHARACTER, WHICH IS THE MORE USEFUL HALF. Every one of the five is pre-1997 and NOT ONE CARRIES A DOI: a 1957 study to determine the specifications of wheelchair ramps; a 1971 architectural movement study whose Part 3 is titled Ramp gradients; a 1979 accessible-buildings study; a 1981 Dutch research paper on accessibility by means of ramps; and a 1993 review of technical requirements for ramps prepared as an attachment to a request for proposals. THIS IS THE FOUNDATION LAYER OF THE WHOLE 1:12 LINEAGE and it is invisible to every DOI-keyed pass this project can run -- the same blind spot that hid REF-01002 for six batches, now showing up as a systematic property of the pre-1990 accessibility literature rather than as one unlucky paper. It also means REF-01002 abstract claim that design recommendations rest on limited empirical research is CHECKABLE against a named set rather than taken on trust. DEPTH-1: nothing discovered here is mined in this pass. || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26 5.2d): mined_ref_id derived -- this row''s own query_text names exactly one REF id that exists in evidence_sources. || RC1/RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26): result-payload link(s) derived from this search''s own query_text against the retrieval log, per section 2.1''s rule. (1 artefact(s)) || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: mined_ref_id set to ''REF-00980'' || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: result artefact(s) added: retrieval-log/session_2026-09-18-research-batch-17-vredenburgh-full-read-and-mining/0bb880bf0ac7b2c5.json', "mined_ref_id" = 'REF-00980' WHERE "exec_id" = 74;
